        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The changed tests cover the named logging and trace paths, but AC-05’s required InvalidOperationException error type is not preserved.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 97,
          "message": "AC-05 requires preserving error.type=invalid-operation, but the processor does not map InvalidOperationException to that allowlisted value.",
          "confidence": 0.96,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RedactingLogProcessor.OnEnd passes exception.GetType().FullName directly to the error.type allowlist, which accepts only lowercase letters, digits, dots, and hyphens.",
            "failureScenario": "When a log has an InvalidOperationException, its type name is System.InvalidOperationException and fails the allowlist, so the required error.type=invalid-operation is omitted. The test uses a custom lowercase exception for the positive case and does not catch this."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
